# .trivyignore — CVE suppression list for the Trivy gate in release.yml.
#
# Trivy fails the release workflow on HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs. This file is the
# escape valve for cases where an upstream image carries a CVE that has no
# fix yet, where the affected code path is provably unreachable, or where
# the vulnerability is otherwise an accepted known limitation.
#
# Format: one CVE id per line. Optional inline comment after `#`.
# Example:
#   CVE-2024-12345  # affects libfoo; we don't link libfoo. 2026-04-25 — gabriel
#
# RULES:
# 1. Every entry MUST have a one-line justification (CVE id, reason, date,
#    reviewer). No silent suppressions.
# 2. Re-evaluate suppressions before each stable release; remove entries
#    where an upstream fix is now available.

# --- Debian Bookworm runtime base image (api, mcp) ----------------------
# All entries below come from `debian:bookworm-slim` and have no fix
# published by the Debian security team as of the v1.0.0 release.
# Re-check before v1.1.0 — see Dockerfile.rust runtime stage.
CVE-2023-45853  # zlib heap overflow; Debian status: will_not_fix (vendor patch declined upstream). Not exploitable in our binaries — we do not pass attacker-controlled input to MiniZip. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2026-0861   # glibc memalign integer overflow; no fix in Debian Bookworm. App does not call memalign with attacker-controlled sizes. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2026-4878   # libcap TOCTOU privilege-escalation race; no fix in Bookworm. We run as non-root uid 10001, no setuid/setcap binaries shipped. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2026-41989  # libgcrypt DoS / buffer overflow; no fix in Bookworm. App does not link or call libgcrypt directly. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2026-33845  # gnutls DTLS zero-length DoS; no fix in Bookworm. App uses rustls (not gnutls) for TLS. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2026-33846  # gnutls heap buffer overflow; no fix in Bookworm. Same rationale as CVE-2026-33845 — gnutls is a transitive package, not a runtime dep. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2026-29111  # systemd arbitrary code execution / DoS; no fix in Bookworm. Container has no systemd in PID 1, ENTRYPOINT is the app binary directly. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2025-69720  # ncurses buffer overflow; no fix in Bookworm. App does not link ncurses. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
